  "resolution": {
    "change": "patches/llvm-mos/0056-llvm-gisel-inline-asm-register-bounds.patch",
    "causal_explanation": "The register-assignment loop advanced through physical class members without validating the requested range, asserting or reading beyond the end. Validate the entire range before assignment and handle failure with DiagnosticInfoInlineAsm. Allocate unconstrained virtual registers independently of the finite physical iterator. Define unused recovery results when a diagnostic handler returns so invalid assembly cannot trigger fallback or undefined virtual-register uses. Only InlineAsmLowering.cpp differs in the isolated baseline/candidate link.",
    "trigger_check": "The original constructed IR still asks for an i128 value in {cc}; its single physical member cannot supply two registers. The runner requires compiler exit 1 and exactly the intended diagnostic. Direct output, input, tied, and indirect-output forms pass all four O0/O2 and abort/fallback configurations, with three valid physical controls and the 1067-test AArch64/ARM/X86 GlobalISel suite.",
